MassPush.extraInfo:
## Java Sample Code
```
MassPushRequest massPushRequest = new MassPushRequest();
massPushRequest.setAppKey(appKey);
List<MassPushRequest.PushTask> pushTasks = new ArrayList<>();
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
    MassPushRequest.PushTask pushTask = new MassPushRequest.PushTask();
    // Push Target
    pushTask.setTarget("DEVICE"); // Push Target: DEVICE: push to devices; ACCOUNT: push to specified accounts; TAG: push to custom tags; ALIAS: push by alias; ALL: broadcast push
    pushTask.setTargetValue("device1,device2,device3"); // Set according to Target. For example, if Target=DEVICE, the corresponding values are device ID 1, device ID 2, etc. Multiple values are separated by commas (up to 100 accounts or devices per request).
    pushTask.setDeviceType("iOS"); // Device type: "iOS" for iOS devices; "ANDROID" for Android devices; "ALL" for all devices (default value).
    // Push Configuration
    pushTask.setPushType("MESSAGE"); // MESSAGE: message (default); NOTICE: notification
    pushTask.setTitle("Hello-" + i); // Title of the message
    pushTask.setBody("PushRequest body" + i); // Content of the message
    // Push Configuration: iOS
    pushTask.setIOSBadge(5); // Badge number on the iOS app icon
    pushTask.setIOSMusic("default"); // Notification sound for iOS
    pushTask.setIOSApnsEnv("PRODUCT"); // iOS notifications are sent via APNs. Specify the environment: 'DEV' for development, 'PRODUCT' for production
    pushTask.setIOSRemind(true); // If the device is offline (i.e., the persistent connection channel with Alibaba Cloud Mobile Push server is disconnected) when the message is pushed, this push will be delivered once as a notification through Apple's APNs. Note: **Converting offline messages to notifications applies only to the `production environment`**
    pushTask.setIOSRemindBody("PushRequest summary"); // Content used for iOS notifications when converting messages to notifications. Only effective when IOSApnsEnv=`PRODUCT` and IOSRemind=true
    pushTask.setIOSExtParameters("{"k1":"ios","k2":"v2"}"); // Extension properties of the notification (Note: This parameter must be passed in JSON map format; otherwise, parsing will fail)
    // Push Configuration: Android
    pushTask.setAndroidOpenType("ACTIVITY"); // Action after clicking the notification: 'APPLICATION': open the application; 'ACTIVITY': open a specific Android Activity; 'URL': open a URL; 'NONE': no redirection
    pushTask.setAndroidNotifyType("SOUND"); // Notification alert method: 'VIBRATE': vibration; 'SOUND': sound; 'DEFAULT': sound and vibration; 'NONE': no handling (customized by the user)
    pushTask.setAndroidOpenUrl("http://www.alibaba.com");
    pushTask.setAndroidMusic("alicloud_notification_sound"); // Notification sound for Huawei OEM channel
    pushTask.setAndroidActivity("com.alibaba.push.PushActivity"); // The Android Activity to open upon receiving the push. Only effective when `AndroidOpenType="ACTIVITY"`
    pushTask.setAndroidPopupActivity("com.alibaba.push.PopupActivity"); // Enables auxiliary popup window functionality. Specifies the Activity to navigate to after clicking the notification (Prerequisites for auxiliary popup: 1. Integration with third-party auxiliary channels; 2. StoreOffline parameter set to true)
    pushTask.setAndroidPopupTitle("Popup Title"); // Title of the auxiliary popup notification
    pushTask.setAndroidPopupBody("Popup Body"); // Content of the auxiliary popup notification
    pushTask.setAndroidNotificationBarType(50); // Custom Android notification bar style, value range: 1–100
    pushTask.setAndroidNotificationBarPriority(2); // Priority of the Android notification in the notification bar: -2, -1, 0, 1, 2
    pushTask.setAndroidExtParameters("{"k1":"android","k2":"v2"}"); // Extension properties of the notification (Note: This parameter must be passed in JSON map format; otherwise, parsing will fail)
    // Push Control
    final Date pushDate = new Date(System.currentTimeMillis() + 3600 * 1000); // For scheduled sending. If not set, the message is sent immediately by default. Time must follow the ISO8601 standard and use UTC time in the format `YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ`.
    final String pushTime = ParameterHelper.getISO8601Time(pushDate);
    pushTask.setPushTime(pushTime); // Delayed push. Optional; if not set, the message is pushed immediately
    pushTask.setStoreOffline(true); // Whether to store offline messages. If enabled, users will receive the message the next time they come online, even if they were offline at the time of pushing
    final String expireTime = ParameterHelper.getISO8601Time(new Date(System.currentTimeMillis() + 12 * 3600 * 1000)); // Message expires after 12 hours and will no longer be sent
    pushTask.setExpireTime(expireTime);
    pushTasks.add(pushTask);
}
massPushRequest.setPushTasks(pushTasks);
MassPushResponse massPushResponse = client.getAcsResponse(massPushRequest);
System.out.printf("RequestId: %s, MessageIds: %s
", massPushResponse.getRequestId(), massPushResponse.getMessageIds().toString());
```
